                <pb facs="0513" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/639: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-19T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 19—6:19
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>819. Legation’s 765, July 27, 6 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Cunningham has requested, August 17, 3 p.m., instructions “to protest
                        individually against all the September 1st taxes,” stating his belief that
                        such protest would have a salutary effect upon the Chinese authorities. I
                        request the Department’s approval of the foregoing.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I am replying as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                            <p>“I assume that the September 1st taxes to which you refer, are those
                                described in your 97, July 26 [<hi rendition="#italic">27?</hi>], 9
                                a.m. If you consider that a protest against these taxes would have a
                                salutary effect upon the Chinese authorities you may, at your
                                discretion, make such a protest either individually or jointly with
                                your colleagues.”</p>
                        </quote></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
